[2026-10-30T13:40:30.251Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"web_search","id":"exec-8bf0c124-8a8a-44cf-8cd9-05ff90868438","query":"graph drawing minimize bends degree one edges port constraints yfiles orthogonal routing ...","action":{"type":"search","queries":["graph drawing minimize bends degree one edges port constraints yfiles orthogonal routing","ELK layered algorithm edge straightening port constraints"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"eclipse.dev","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"# ELK Layered ... Layer-based algorithm provided by the Eclipse Layout Kernel. ... Additional Port Space | `new ElkMargin(0)` ... BK Edge Straightening | `EdgeStraighteningStrategy.IMPROVE_STRAIGHTNES","title":"ELK Layered (ELK)","url":"https://eclipse.dev/elk/reference/algorithms/org-eclipse-elk-layered.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.yworks.com","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"yFiles allows port constraints, which let you control exactly where an edge connects to a node (top, bottom, left, right, or specific ports). ... How","title":"yWorks - FAQ","url":"https://www.yworks.com/faq?id=1065"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"eclipse.dev","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"If you wish to constrain the ports have a look at the `portConstraints` property and this example. ... The `layerConstraint` property allows constraining a node","title":"Layered: Constraining the Model (ELK)","url":"https://eclipse.dev/elk/blog/posts/2023/23-01-09-constraining-the-model.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"# ELK Layered Support for routing to optimal node port #916 ... * We do not specify the source / target port of an edge","title":"ELK Layered Support for routing to optimal node port · Issue #916 · eclipse-elk/elk · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/eclipse-elk/elk/issues/916"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"elk.models.nasdanika.org","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"* Ensure `algorithm` is set to `org.eclipse.elk.layered` before applying layered-prefixed options — otherwise layered-specific keys might not influence the actual algorithm choice or ordering. ...","title":"Eclipse Layout Kernel","url":"https://elk.models.nasdanika.org/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"eclipse.dev","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"The layered algorithm or Sugiyama algorithm is in its implementation in ELK divided into five phases with intermediate processing slots: Cycle Breaking, Layer Assignment, Crossing","title":"Layered (overview) (ELK)","url":"https://eclipse.dev/elk/blog/posts/2025/25-08-21-layered.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"rtsys.informatik.uni-kiel.de","ref_id":"turn0search12","snippet":"** There are two *port constraints* relevant for our use case (for other constraints used in ELK Layered see Schulze et al. ... **Definition 13","title":"2. Preliminaries","url":"https://rtsys.informatik.uni-kiel.de/~biblio/downloads/theses/alan-mt.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.yfiles.com","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"This mode produces orthogonal edge routes and maintains the original node size. ... If enabled, the algorithm may insert additional bends to obtain a more","title":"Orthogonal Layout | yFiles for HTML Docs","url":"https://docs.yfiles.com/yfiles-html/dguide/orthogonal_layout/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.yfiles.com","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"Image: extended by y.layout.router.OrthogonalEdgeRouter ... This edge routing algorithm generates orthogonal routes for the edges of the graph. Note that class `EdgeRouter` offers a newer,","title":"OrthogonalEdgeRouter (yFiles-2.19 API)","url":"https://docs.yfiles.com/yfiles/doc/api-svg/y/layout/router/OrthogonalEdgeRouter.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.yworks.com","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"Not only will it find a way but also one with fewest possible changes in direction. ... Monotonic edge paths are useful, for example, when","title":"Orthogonal Edge Routing","url":"https://docs.yworks.com/yfiles/doc/developers-guide/orthogonal_edge_router.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.yworks.com","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"* Orthogonalization – The bends and the angles are computed. ... OrthogonalLayout tries to optimize diverse objective functions such as bend minimization, number of edge","title":"OrthogonalLayout | yFiles for HTML Docs","url":"https://docs.yworks.com/yfiles-html/api/OrthogonalLayout/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"\"elk.algorithm\": \"layered\", ... `elk.portConstraints` | `UNDEFINED` | Port constraint level: `UNDEFINED`, `FREE`, `FIXED_SIDE`, `FIXED_ORDER`, `FIXED_POS` ... `elk.layered.layering.strategy` | `LONGES","title":"GitHub - depetrol/pyelk · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/depetrol/pyelk"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.sciencedirect.com","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"# Layered drawing of undirected graphs with generalized port constraints ... Since the framework assumes directed graphs, we propose several ways to orient the edges","title":"Layered drawing of undirected graphs with generalized port constraints - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0925772122000293"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"publikationen.uni-tuebingen.de","ref_id":"turn0search13","snippet":"Incorporating Port/Side Constraints ... lowing approach which produces port constraint preserving odevs drawings ... one bend as shown in Fig. ... into the placement strategy","title":"Orthogonal Graph Drawing","url":"https://publikationen.uni-tuebingen.de/xmlui/bitstream/10900/49366/1/pdf/diss.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"rtsys.informatik.uni-kiel.de","ref_id":"turn0search14","snippet":"for the second layer of the graph in Fig. 3 while keeping the vertices of the third ... For each dummy vertex vi, i ∈{2,","title":"Port Constraints in Hierarchical Layout","url":"https://rtsys.informatik.uni-kiel.de/~biblio/downloads/papers/gd09.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"arxiv.org","ref_id":"turn0academia15","snippet":"Orthogonal drawings, i.e., embeddings of graphs into grids, are a classic topic in Graph Drawing. ... A key ingredient for bend minimization algorithms is the","title":"Efficient Algorithms for Ortho-Radial Graph Drawing","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.05048"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"arxiv.org","ref_id":"turn0academia16","snippet":"Orthogonal graph drawing has many applications, e.g., for laying out UML diagrams or cableplans. In this paper, we present a new pipeline that draws multigraphs","title":"A Simple Pipeline for Orthogonal Graph Drawing","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.01671"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"arxiv.org","ref_id":"turn0academia17","snippet":"Title: Layered Drawing of Undirected Graphs with Generalized Port Constraints ... Since the framework assumes directed graphs, we propose several ways to orient the edges","title":"Layered Drawing of Undirected Graphs with Generalized Port Constraints","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.10583"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"arxiv.org","ref_id":"turn0academia18","snippet":"Let $G$ be a planar $3$-graph (i.e., a planar graph with vertex degree at most three) with $n$ vertices. We present the first $O(n^2)$-time algorithm","title":"Bend-minimum Orthogonal Drawings in Quadratic Time","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.05813"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search19","snippet":"In graph drawing styles that represent the edges of a graph by polylines (sequences of line segments connected at bends), it is desirable to minimize","title":"Bend minimization","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bend_minimization"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search20","snippet":"However, these problems also differ in several important ways: for instance, in EDA, area minimization and signal length are more important than aesthetics, and the","title":"Graph drawing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_drawing"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search21","snippet":"Simultaneous embedding is a technique in graph drawing and information visualization for visualizing two or more different graphs on the same or overlapping sets of","title":"Simultaneous embedding","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simultaneous_embedding"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search22","snippet":"Their purpose is to position the nodes of a graph in two-dimensional or three-dimensional space so that all the edges are of more or less","title":"Force-directed graph drawing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Force-directed_graph_drawing"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search23","snippet":"However, graphs often contain cycles, minimizing the number of inconsistently oriented edges is NP-hard, and minimizing the number of crossings is also NP-hard; so, layered","title":"Layered graph drawing","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Layered_graph_drawing"}]}}
