[2026-10-30T13:55:22.259Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat docs/case-studies/issue-41/data/issue.json; cat experiments/issue-41-reciprocal.mjs; cat experiments/issue-41-sheet.mjs; cat .gitignore; sed -n '1,260p' .github/workflows/github-pages.yml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41\",\"id\":6119680818,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDON1sLX88AAAABbMLrMg\",\"number\":41,\"title\":\"Continue to make links network rendering even more perfect\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"konard\",\"id\":1431904,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/konard\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[{\"id\":8113453895,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDON1sLX88AAAAB45l7Rw\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Something isn't working\",\"archived_at\":null,\"archived_by\":null}],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T13:10:19Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T13:18:10Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"OWNER\",\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"For https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0222 default layout should be like this https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0222&turns=0+-30\\n\\nWe should double check all other applicable places.\\n\\nSo by default when link has no start, and single end or vice versa, we should prefer in the layout simplest possible solution.\\n\\nAnd with auto gap reduction algorithm after application of 30 degree turn it works perfectly.\\n\\nFor https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0112 we should use https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0112&turns=%2C-30+0 and so on.\\n\\nDouble check more 20 random cases on 1-3 links. And make sure we prefer the most simple and perfect solution for default links arrangements possible.\\n\\nHere we don't touch gaps configuration (that is responsibility of automatic gap reduction algorithm), only turns and default placement of the links, where applicable.\\n\\nWe should carefully consider not to break previous perfect behavior, but we should not bend the line if there is a straight line can be.\\n\\nOther examples (where I had to make adjustments to make it perfect): \\n\\n- https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0001&turns=%2C0+-30\\n- https://konard.github.io/network/?code=2002&turns=-30+0\\n\\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\\n\\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\\n\\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\\n\\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null}import { writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { createServer } from 'vite';\nimport { reported, randomNetworks } from './issue-41-cases.mjs';\nconst server = await createServer({ server: { middlewareMode: true }, appType: 'custom' });\ntry {\n  const { decode } = await server.ssrLoadModule('/src/links/configurations.js');\n  const { normalizeStyle, shapeOfStyle } = await server.ssrLoadModule('/src/links/style.js');\n  const { overlapCost } = await server.ssrLoadModule('/src/links/collisions.js');\n  const results = [];\n  for (const { code } of [...reported, ...randomNetworks().map((code) => ({ code }))]) {\n    const links = decode(code.match(/../g).join(' '));\n    const base = shapeOfStyle(normalizeStyle(), links);\n    const variants = {};\n    for (const kind of ['all', 'first', 'none']) {\n      const turns = base.turns.map((pair, i) =>\n        pair.map((angle, end) => {\n          const ref = links[i][end];\n          if (ref && links[ref - 1].includes(i + 1) && (kind === 'none' || (kind === 'first' && i > ref - 1))) return 0;\n          return angle;\n        }),\n      );\n      variants[kind] = { turns, cost: overlapCost(links, { ...base, turns }) };\n    }\n    results.push({ code, variants });\n  }\n  await writeFile(\n    'docs/case-studies/issue-41/data/reciprocal-experiment.json',\n    JSON.stringify(results, null, 2) + '\\n',\n  );\n  results.forEach(({ code, variants }) =>\n    console.log(code, Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(variants).map(([key, value]) => [key, value.cost]))),\n  );\n} finally {\n  await server.close();\n}\nimport { readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { chromium } from 'playwright';\nconst root = 'docs/case-studies/issue-41';\nconst before = JSON.parse(await readFile(`${root}/data/chromium-before.json`, 'utf8')).networks;\nconst after = JSON.parse(await readFile(`${root}/data/chromium-after.json`, 'utf8')).networks;\nconst browser = await chromium.launch();\ntry {\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1320, height: 1000 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\n  for (let part = 0; part < 2; part++) {\n    const cards = after.slice(part * 12, (part + 1) * 12).map(({ code, svg }) => {\n      const original = before.find((item) => item.code === code).svg;\n      return `<article><h2>${code}</h2><div><figure>${original}<figcaption>Before</figcaption></figure><figure>${svg}<figcaption>After</figcaption></figure></div></article>`;\n    }).join('');\n    const html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Issue 41 before/after ${part + 1}</title><style>body{margin:16px;background:#101420;color:#fff;font:14px system-ui}main{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px}article{border:1px solid #586178;border-radius:8px;padding:8px}h2{font:16px monospace;margin:0 0 8px}article div{display:flex;gap:8px}figure{flex:1;margin:0;min-width:0}svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}figcaption{text-align:center;margin-top:4px}</style><h1>Issue 41: four reported cases and twenty seeded 1–3-link networks (${part + 1}/2)</h1><main>${cards}</main></html>`;\n    await writeFile(`${root}/data/comparison-${part + 1}.html`, html);\n    await page.setContent(html);\n    await page.screenshot({ path: `${root}/screenshots/comparison-${part + 1}.png`, fullPage: true });\n  }\n} finally {\n  await browser.close();\n}\n# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.\n\n# dependencies\n/node_modules\n/.pnp\n.pnp.js\n\n# testing\n/coverage\n\n# production\n/build\n\n# misc\n.DS_Store\n.env.local\n.env.development.local\n.env.test.local\n.env.production.local\n\nnpm-debug.log*\nyarn-debug.log*\nyarn-error.log*\n\n# playwright\n/.playwright-mcp\n\n# contact sheets and screenshots written by experiments/contact-sheet.mjs\n/experiments/out\n\n# Python/tool and generated CI evidence\n__pycache__/\n.ruff_cache/\n/browser-results/\n/lychee/\n/.lycheecache\nname: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  workflow_dispatch:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '0 6 * * 1'\n\n# Least-privilege default; only the deploy job may publish to Pages.\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\n# actions/checkout runs `git init` before any step can configure Git; this\n# silences its \"default branch name\" hint.\nenv:\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: init.defaultBranch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n\njobs:\n  prepare:\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-prepare\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      pages: read\n    outputs:\n      code: ${{ steps.changes.outputs.code }}\n      docs: ${{ steps.changes.outputs.docs }}\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout the merge result\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '24.x'\n      - name: Verify merge freshness and detect changes\n        id: changes\n        run: node scripts/ci-changes.mjs\n      - name: Check GitHub Pages configuration before building\n        run: node scripts/check-pages.mjs\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: [REDACTED] github.token }}\n          REQUIRE_PAGES: ${{ github.event_name != 'pull_request' && 'true' || 'false' }}\n\n  # Lint the workflows themselves (actionlint also runs shellcheck on run: blocks).\n  lint-workflows:\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-lint-workflows\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout source\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Run actionlint\n        uses: docker://rhysd/actionlint@sha256:b1934ee5f1c509618f2508e6eb47ee0d3520686341fec936f3b79331f9315667 # v1.7.12\n        with:\n          args: -color\n\n  # Fast checks run before the tests and the build.\n  checks:\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-checks\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    needs: prepare\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout source\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '24.x'\n          cache: npm\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Lint\n        run: npm run lint\n\n      - name: Check formatting\n        run: npm run format:check\n\n      - name: Check file size limits\n        run: npm run check:file-size\n\n      - name: Check for secrets\n        run: npm run check:secrets\n\n      - name: Audit dependencies\n        run: npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=moderate\n\n  test:\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-test\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    needs: [prepare, lint-workflows, checks, network-browsers]\n    if: needs.prepare.outputs.code == 'true'\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 20\n\n    steps:\n      # On pull requests this is the merge result with main, not the branch head.\n      - name: Checkout source\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '24.x'\n          cache: npm\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Run tests\n        run: npm run test:ci\n\n      - name: Build the React app\n        run: npm run build\n\n      # Issue #11: every CV (position × style × language) is printed to PDF by\n      # headless Chromium and checked: at most 2 pages for a position, 1 page\n      # for the compact style, and a text layer an ATS can read.\n      - name: Install Chromium for the CV PDFs\n        run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium\n\n      - name: Print the CV PDFs\n        run: npm run build:cv\n\n      # GitHub Pages is set to deploy from GitHub Actions, so the site is\n      # published from this artifact, not from a branch or the docs/ folder.\n      # Pull requests upload it too, so a broken artifact fails before merge.\n      - name: Upload the build as the Pages artifact with bounded transport retries\n        uses: ./.github/actions/upload-artifact\n        with:\n          name: github-pages\n          path: build/\n          pages: 'true'\n\n  network-browsers:\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-network-browsers-${{ matrix.engine }}\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    needs: [prepare, lint-workflows, checks, tooling]\n    if: needs.prepare.outputs.code == 'true'\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        include:\n          - engine: chromium\n            os: ubuntu-24.04\n          - engine: firefox\n            os: ubuntu-24.04\n          # This container's Linux GTK renderer omits backdrop effects on\n          # screen. Test WebKit on macOS, the platform used by the reported bug.\n          # Pin Intel: ARM capacity left a previous job without any runner.\n          - engine: webkit\n            os: macos-15-intel\n    env:\n      ENGINE: ${{ matrix.engine }}\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout source\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v7\n        with:\n          node-version: '24.x'\n          cache: npm\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Build the editor\n        run: npm run build\n\n      - name: Install the browser\n        id: browser\n        # WebKit uses macOS because Linux GTK can stall on glass panels.\n        # https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/43426\n        run: npx playwright install --with-deps \"$ENGINE\"\n\n      - name: Initialize browser evidence\n        run: |\n          mkdir -p browser-results\n          node -e 'require(\"node:fs\").writeFileSync(\"browser-results/run.json\", JSON.stringify({sha: process.env.GITHUB_SHA, engine: process.env.ENGINE}))'\n\n      - name: Verify existing editor features and image downloads\n        run: npm run test:network:browser\n        env:\n          CAPTURE_DIR: browser-results/screenshots/editor\n\n      - name: Verify history, self loops, layouts, clipboard and mobile editing\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.browser.outcome == 'success' }}\n        run: npm run test:network:issue19\n        env:\n          CAPTURE_DIR: browser-results/screenshots/issue19\n          RESULT_DIR: browser-results/data/issue19\n\n      - name: Verify editor geometry, source colors and shared settings\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.browser.outcome == 'success' }}\n        run: npm run test:network:issue21\n        env:\n          CAPTURE_DIR: browser-results/screenshots/issue21\n          RESULT_DIR: browser-results/data/issue21\n\n      - name: Verify curved markers, per-link gaps and bounded gallery blur surfaces\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.browser.outcome == 'success' }}\n        # Capture the actual compositor, including Firefox backdrop effects.\n        run: |\n          if [[ \"$RUNNER_OS\" == \"macOS\" ]]; then\n            DISPLAY_CAPTURE=1 npm run test:network:issue23\n          else\n            mkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$XWD_FILE\")\"\n            xvfb-run -a -s \"-screen 0 1600x1200x24 -fbdir $(dirname \"$XWD_FILE\")\" npm run test:network:issue23\n          fi\n        env:\n          CARD_BATCHES: '8' # The exact reported 4,131-card load, in every engine.\n          XWD_FILE: ${{ runner.temp }}/issue23-display/Xvfb_screen0\n          CAPTURE_DIR: browser-results/screenshots/issue23\n          RESULT_DIR: browser-results/data/issue23\n\n      - name: Verify automatic spacing, sharp balanced arrows and per-link cards\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.browser.outcome == 'success' }}\n        run: npm run test:network:issue25\n        env:\n          CAPTURE_DIR: browser-results/screenshots/issue25\n          RESULT_DIR: browser-results/data/issue25\n\n      - name: Verify equal closed gaps, historical URLs and numeric keyboard controls\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.browser.outcome == 'success' }}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
