[2026-10-30T13:58:36.222Z] [STDERR] +# Issue 41: simpler default reference turns
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.225Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.228Z] [STDERR] +The four reported networks now open with exactly the same geometry as the
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.230Z] [STDERR] +owner's manually corrected links. Aligned references use straight shafts by
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.231Z] [STDERR] +default. Their resolved turns appear in the existing controls and feed the
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.233Z] [STDERR] +preview, spacing worker, Apply, shared links and image exports.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.235Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.237Z] [STDERR] +This addresses [issue 41](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41)
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.238Z] [STDERR] +in [PR 42](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/42). The complete
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.242Z] [STDERR] +[requirement inventory](REQUIREMENTS.md) maps each request to its implementation
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.245Z] [STDERR] +and evidence. [PLAN.md](PLAN.md) tracks completion.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.246Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.249Z] [STDERR] +## Evidence and timeline
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.251Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.253Z] [STDERR] +All times are UTC on 30 October 2026 unless stated otherwise.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.255Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.257Z] [STDERR] +| Time | Event and evidence |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.259Z] [STDERR] +| --- | --- |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.261Z] [STDERR] +| 29 October | PR 36 introduced continuous middles. Its geometry is inherited by the current renderer. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.266Z] [STDERR] +| 12:42:32 | [PR 38](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/38) merged local spacing with fixed positions, self-crossing checks and background solving. See `data/pr-38.json`. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.268Z] [STDERR] +| 13:10:19 | Issue 41 opened with unnecessary bending in default networks. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.269Z] [STDERR] +| 13:18:10 | Latest issue edit supplied four corrections and requested twenty more cases, preservation of previous good behavior, and this case study. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.270Z] [STDERR] +| 13:39:27 | Draft PR 42 created on the prepared issue branch. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.272Z] [STDERR] +| 13:39:31 | Initial CI run 41065058961 started on `df3567f`; it passed. Its complete log is preserved in `logs/ci-initial.log`. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.273Z] [STDERR] +| Investigation | Archived the issue, every issue/PR comment endpoint, reviews, sub-issues and recent related PRs. Initial feedback and sub-issue arrays were empty. Reproduced all four examples with failing tests and Chromium screenshots before implementing the correction. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.275Z] [STDERR] +| Implementation | Compared unrestricted straightening with reciprocal-route preservation; retained existing reciprocal curves after the measured overlap regressions below. Added shared default inference, explicit-zero preservation and topology-aware control resets. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.276Z] [STDERR] +| Verification | Captured default/manual equality, twenty unchanged seeded samples, mobile editing, Apply/share and real SVG downloads. Local and current-head CI results are recorded below and in the final validation metadata. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.278Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.281Z] [STDERR] +The API responses are in [data/](data/), including the complete issue body and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.284Z] [STDERR] +the three distinct PR feedback endpoints. Local commands and CI output are in
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.286Z] [STDERR] +[logs/](logs/). Intermediate failures are retained as investigation evidence;
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.290Z] [STDERR] +files with `draft`, `candidate` or `before` in their names describe earlier states.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.295Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.298Z] [STDERR] +## Reproduction and root cause
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.300Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.302Z] [STDERR] +On the parent implementation, open `/network/?code=0222`. The first link's free
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.304Z] [STDERR] +half and middle already follow the chord toward link 2, but its target approach
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.306Z] [STDERR] +is still rotated by the nominal 30° angle. Adding `&turns=0+-30` cancels that
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.307Z] [STDERR] +rotation and makes the reference straight. The other three supplied examples
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.309Z] [STDERR] +exercise the opposite end and references next to a self-closed half:
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.310Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.313Z] [STDERR] +| Code | Expected editable turns |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.314Z] [STDERR] +| --- | --- |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.317Z] [STDERR] +| `0222` | `0 -30` |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.319Z] [STDERR] +| `0112` | `0 0,-30 0` |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.320Z] [STDERR] +| `0001` | `0 0,0 -30` |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.321Z] [STDERR] +| `2002` | `-30 0` |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.322Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.323Z] [STDERR] +`glyph.linkCurve` already chooses a middle tangent using the reference chord.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.324Z] [STDERR] +The editor's fixed endpoint angles independently add 30° in `approach`.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.325Z] [STDERR] +Previously `style.linkTurns` supplied zero for every unspecified turn, so the
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.326Z] [STDERR] +nominal angle remained even when a straight reference was feasible. This is a
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.328Z] [STDERR] +default-selection defect in this repository, with no external library defect.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.329Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.330Z] [STDERR] +The reproducing run in `logs/regression-before.log` failed all four supplied
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.332Z] [STDERR] +geometry comparisons, applicable random samples, a straight through-link and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.334Z] [STDERR] +the explicit-zero distinction. The baseline screenshots and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.335Z] [STDERR] +`data/chromium-before.json` preserve the actual picture and controls.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.336Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.337Z] [STDERR] +Two secondary consequences needed explicit handling. Normalization used to
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.338Z] [STDERR] +discard an all-zero turn list, conflating a deliberate manual choice with an
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.340Z] [STDERR] +unspecified default. Also, individual turn resets assumed zero. With inferred
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.342Z] [STDERR] +defaults, these would change a shared/applied drawing or reset a field to the
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.344Z] [STDERR] +wrong value. A nonempty zero list now survives normalization and sharing;
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.347Z] [STDERR] +individual reset buttons use the current topology's resolved default. A blank
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.348Z] [STDERR] +numeric editing draft continues to preserve the current turn. Reference edits
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.349Z] [STDERR] +and removals recompute defaults while explicit turn lists retain their values.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.351Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.352Z] [STDERR] +## Solution and scope
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.353Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.354Z] [STDERR] +`glyph.defaultTurns` uses the existing layout and endpoint directions. For each
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.357Z] [STDERR] +non-self reference it checks that the chord follows the link's middle tangent,
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.359Z] [STDERR] +then returns the ordinary integer turn that aligns the endpoint with that
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.362Z] [STDERR] +chord. No separate solver or alternate geometry is introduced. It applies to
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.364Z] [STDERR] +either end, a reference beside a closed half, and collinear through-links.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.367Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.369Z] [STDERR] +The rule preserves deliberate angle/bend settings, lens geometry, self-closed
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.370Z] [STDERR] +halves and reciprocal routes. Straightening both sides of a reciprocal pair
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.373Z] [STDERR] +collapses two shafts onto the same chord. A finite
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.379Z] [STDERR] +[experiment](../../../experiments/issue-41-reciprocal.mjs) compared all eligible
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.381Z] [STDERR] +ends, only the first reciprocal direction, and keeping reciprocal curves.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.383Z] [STDERR] +For `2012` the respective existing overlap scores were 33.013, 6.906 and 0.881;
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.385Z] [STDERR] +for `1212` they were 35.260, 8.795 and 0.800. Preserving those curves meets the
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.387Z] [STDERR] +request to retain previous good behavior. Full results are in
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.389Z] [STDERR] +`data/reciprocal-experiment.json`; the rejected candidate's browser and geometry
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.391Z] [STDERR] +measurements are retained separately.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.394Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.396Z] [STDERR] +All production `shapeOfStyle` and `linkTurns` consumers now pass the actual
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.399Z] [STDERR] +links. The renderer, editor controls and worker therefore resolve the same
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.400Z] [STDERR] +starting turns. The count-only overload retains zero defaults for existing
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.401Z] [STDERR] +geometry callers without topology. Legacy gallery/rain glyphs retain their
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.403Z] [STDERR] +deliberate mirrored, bulged appearance; the inherited historical digest checks
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.404Z] [STDERR] +that path. No placement, gap configuration, middle-cut rule, collision scoring
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.405Z] [STDERR] +or automatic gap-reduction implementation changed.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.406Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.408Z] [STDERR] +The existing solver may still change a default turn while reducing marker
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.410Z] [STDERR] +collisions. Existing fixed-position crossings or marker clearances are not
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.412Z] [STDERR] +claimed to vanish. `data/measurements.json` separates default geometry from the
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.413Z] [STDERR] +optional spacing result and records every configured gap. The scorer includes
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.414Z] [STDERR] +a tiny turn regularizer, so a 30° correction adds `0.00003` even to an otherwise
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.415Z] [STDERR] +clear drawing; that is not a painted collision.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.417Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.420Z] [STDERR] +## Twenty additional cases and visual review
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.422Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.424Z] [STDERR] +The sample generator uses seed `0x41c0de` and samples without replacement: all
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.425Z] [STDERR] +four one-link networks, eight two-link networks and eight three-link networks.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.429Z] [STDERR] +The sample is fixed before reviewing results; difficult cases are retained.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.430Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.434Z] [STDERR] +| Links | Codes | Review |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.436Z] [STDERR] +| --- | --- | --- |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.438Z] [STDERR] +| 1 | `00`, `01`, `10`, `11` | Free segments and self loops retain their original geometry. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.439Z] [STDERR] +| 2 | `2211`, `0111`, `2202`, `1120`, `2012`, `0010`, `1212`, `1002` | Simplify eligible single references; preserve reciprocal routes and loops. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.440Z] [STDERR] +| 3 | `020313`, `122101`, `121310`, `313322`, `011111`, `033310`, `202221`, `021023` | Apply the same rule at either end, preserving link order, colors, middles and closed halves. Existing crossings remain the spacing solver's responsibility. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.442Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.444Z] [STDERR] +These comparison sheets include the four reported networks first, followed by
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.445Z] [STDERR] +all twenty additional samples. Each card shows the parent default on the left
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.446Z] [STDERR] +and the corrected default on the right. Every individual native screenshot is
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.447Z] [STDERR] +also committed in [screenshots/](screenshots/).
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.450Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.451Z] [STDERR] +![Before and after: reported examples and first random samples](screenshots/comparison-1.png)
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.452Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.454Z] [STDERR] +![Before and after: remaining random samples](screenshots/comparison-2.png)
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.456Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.459Z] [STDERR] +Raw SVG, path data, controls, browser versions and page errors are preserved in
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.461Z] [STDERR] +`data/chromium-before.json`, `data/chromium-after.json` and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.462Z] [STDERR] +`data/firefox-after.json`. Exact SVG equality verifies all four requested manual
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.464Z] [STDERR] +arrangements, default sharing, Apply, applied sharing and the actual downloaded
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.466Z] [STDERR] +SVG. Mobile screenshots verify a 390px viewport without horizontal overflow.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.467Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.468Z] [STDERR] +## Alternatives and external research
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.474Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.477Z] [STDERR] +Primary documentation was consulted on 30 October 2026; findings and decisions
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.478Z] [STDERR] +are archived in [data/research.json](data/research.json).
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.480Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.482Z] [STDERR] +| Component | Relevant capability | Decision |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.484Z] [STDERR] +| --- | --- | --- |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.487Z] [STDERR] +| [ELK Layered](https://eclipse.dev/elk/reference/algorithms/org-eclipse-elk-layered.html) | Straight, orthogonal and spline routing with port constraints and edge-straightening options | Confirms straightness can be a separate objective. A replacement layout engine would unnecessarily change established link geometry and positions. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.495Z] [STDERR] +| [yFiles OrthogonalEdgeRouter](https://docs.yworks.com/yfiles/doc/developers-guide/orthogonal_edge_router.html) | Routes between fixed nodes with few changes in direction and independent spacing controls | Supports separating routing simplicity from clearance. Orthogonal segments do not match the continuous doublet geometry. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.497Z] [STDERR] +| Existing `glyph`, `style`, `d3-force` and gap reducer | Shared geometry, stable placement, editable turns and painted-shape spacing already implemented | Reuse these components; no added dependency. |
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.498Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.500Z] [STDERR] +A code-specific special case for the four URLs would miss other topologies and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.501Z] [STDERR] +placements. Making every reference straight would collapse reciprocal routes
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.502Z] [STDERR] +and spoil lenses. Altering all nominal angles would change intentional manual
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.504Z] [STDERR] +settings and gallery glyphs. The chosen rule checks geometric feasibility at
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.506Z] [STDERR] +the shared default boundary. The reproducible root cause provides sufficient
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.508Z] [STDERR] +evidence; existing opt-in `solveDebug` diagnostics remain off by default.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.509Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.510Z] [STDERR] +## Verification and reproduction commands
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.511Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.512Z] [STDERR] +The focused tests cover the four requested turns, twenty fixed samples, every
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.514Z] [STDERR] +one- to three-link topology (4,181 networks), eight placement modes with rotated
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.520Z] [STDERR] +and reordered coordinates, explicit/manual turns, defaults after reference
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.522Z] [STDERR] +edits, numeric drafts and resets. Exhaustive assertions preserve raw middles,
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.523Z] [STDERR] +every free/self half and configured gaps. Existing integration tests now pass
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.526Z] [STDERR] +the same topology to their solver and renderer instead of mixing count-only
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.528Z] [STDERR] +zero turns with inferred turns.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.529Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.530Z] [STDERR] +```sh
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.532Z] [STDERR] +npm ci
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.536Z] [STDERR] +npx vitest run src/links/issue-41.test.js src/pages/network-41.test.jsx
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.538Z] [STDERR] +npm run test:ci
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.544Z] [STDERR] +npm run check
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.545Z] [STDERR] +npm run build
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.549Z] [STDERR] +npm run test:network:issue41
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.551Z] [STDERR] +ENGINE=firefox npm run test:network:issue41
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.553Z] [STDERR] +node experiments/issue-41-measure.mjs
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.555Z] [STDERR] +node experiments/issue-41-reciprocal.mjs
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.557Z] [STDERR] +node experiments/issue-41-perfect.mjs
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.560Z] [STDERR] +node experiments/issue-41-sheet.mjs
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.563Z] [STDERR] +bash experiments/issue-41-regressions.sh chromium firefox
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.565Z] [STDERR] +```
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.567Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.569Z] [STDERR] +Use `CAPTURE_DIR` and `RESULT_DIR` to keep subsequent browser results outside
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.572Z] [STDERR] +the committed historical evidence. `PHASE=before` records a baseline against a
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.573Z] [STDERR] +parent build without requiring default/manual equality. The bounded audit and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.575Z] [STDERR] +measurements run sequentially; they do not stress the host's stack or memory.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.576Z] [STDERR] +The browser harness always closes its browser and preview server.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.577Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.579Z] [STDERR] +CI runs the new browser contract on Chromium/Linux, Firefox/Linux and
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.583Z] [STDERR] +WebKit/macOS alongside all inherited editor suites, including the full
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.584Z] [STDERR] +4,131-card gallery load. Unit tests, static/tooling checks, build, PDFs and link
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.587Z] [STDERR] +checks remain enabled. This private site's package has no automatic versioned
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.589Z] [STDERR] +release workflow, so no release version change is needed.
[2026-10-30T13:58:36.591Z] [STDERR] +
