[2026-10-30T14:42:22.168Z] [STDOUT] {"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/events","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41","id":6119680818,"node_id":"I_kwDON1sLX88AAAABbMLrMg","number":41,"title":"Continue to make links network rendering even more perfect","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8113453895,"node_id":"LA_kwDON1sLX88AAAAB45l7Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-30T13:10:19Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T13:18:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"For https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0222 default layout should be like this https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0222&turns=0+-30\n\nWe should double check all other applicable places.\n\nSo by default when link has no start, and single end or vice versa, we should prefer in the layout simplest possible solution.\n\nAnd with auto gap reduction algorithm after application of 30 degree turn it works perfectly.\n\nFor https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0112 we should use https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0112&turns=%2C-30+0 and so on.\n\nDouble check more 20 random cases on 1-3 links. And make sure we prefer the most simple and perfect solution for default links arrangements possible.\n\nHere we don't touch gaps configuration (that is responsibility of automatic gap reduction algorithm), only turns and default placement of the links, where applicable.\n\nWe should carefully consider not to break previous perfect behavior, but we should not bend the line if there is a straight line can be.\n\nOther examples (where I had to make adjustments to make it perfect): \n\n- https://konard.github.io/network/?code=0001&turns=%2C0+-30\n- https://konard.github.io/network/?code=2002&turns=-30+0\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/41/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/42","id":5085255613,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABLxrXvQ","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/42","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/42.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/42.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/42","number":42,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prefer straight default turns for aligned link references","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Opening `0222`, `0112`, `0001` or `2002` now produces exactly the owner's corrected arrangement without entering manual turns. Aligned references use straight default turns, with the same resolved values in the controls, renderer, spacing worker and image exports.\n\nThe geometric rule also handles other single references and collinear through-links. It preserves reciprocal routes, lenses, closed halves, intentional angles/bends and legacy gallery geometry. Explicit turns, including an all-zero list, survive Apply and sharing; individual resets restore the current network's default. Gap configuration, placement and the gap-reduction algorithm are unchanged.\n\nFixes #41\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\n- Before: open `/network/?code=0222`; its target approach bends unnecessarily. Entering `turns=0 -30` removes the bend. The other three supplied URLs reproduce the symmetric cases.\n- Automated regression: `src/links/issue-41.test.js` compares all four supplied arrangements, checks twenty seeded 1–3-link networks and audits every one of the 4,181 small topologies, including fixed middles, free/self halves and unchanged gaps. Editor tests cover turns, numeric drafts, resets, sharing and topology edits.\n- All 977 unit tests pass. ESLint, Prettier, file limits, secret scanning, Python/Ruff/ShellCheck and the production build pass locally.\n- Chromium, Firefox and WebKit/macOS pass the new browser contract: 24 networks, exact default/manual SVG equality, sharing, native editing, worker spacing, Apply, real SVG download and mobile layout. All inherited browser suites also pass in CI. A final Playwright MCP review verifies native keyboard editing, resets and unchanged gaps with desktop/mobile screenshots.\n- A separate exhaustive painted-collision audit preserves all 141 previously collision-free default drawings among the 4,181 topologies. A reciprocal-routing experiment explains why those established curves are retained.\n\nThe [case study](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-41-ebf5585c69b9/docs/case-studies/issue-41/README.md) contains the complete requirement inventory, timeline, root causes, primary-source component research, solution decisions, raw data, before/after screenshots and reproducible commands. Remaining crossings in fixed layouts remain subject to the existing optional spacing solver.\n\nThe complete [implementation CI run](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/41068595873) passed. Its full log, metadata and three-engine browser data are committed in the case study. The [final CI run](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/41071404057) also passed on the exact final head `d0362f1`: all three browser engines, 977 unit tests, static/tooling/security checks, documentation, production build, CV PDFs and pipeline status. The branch includes the latest `main` and has a clean worktree. The case study also records a local runner parsing error after all 18 individual suites succeeded, and the corrected runner’s syntax/ShellCheck validation.\n\n### Before and after\n\nEach card shows the original default on the left and corrected default on the right. The first four cards are the reported examples; the remaining twenty are the unchanged seeded sample.\n\n![Before/after: reported cases and first random samples](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-41-ebf5585c69b9/docs/case-studies/issue-41/screenshots/comparison-1.png?raw=true)\n\n![Before/after: remaining random samples](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-41-ebf5585c69b9/docs/case-studies/issue-41/screenshots/comparison-2.png?raw=true)\n","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:39:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T14:42:16Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"19cc84fd54a84762f212756280312f5cf8e82b90","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/42/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/42/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/42/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/d0362f1bb770403c5f1ba70b90962ba59da4a76d","head":{"label":"konard:issue-41-ebf5585c69b9","ref":"issu